<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 180,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 of barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 180,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 of barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 40,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 80,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 60,000 tonnes of Australian wheat and 60,000 tonnes of Canadian barley at its weekly tender, all for April shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 40,000	   Western white	    20,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter</p>
<p>				    (11.5 percent protein)20,000</p>
<p> Canada     80,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								  64,000</p>
<p>				   Durum			16,000</p>
<p> Australia  60,000	   Standard white	   40,000</p>
<p>				   Prime Hard		 20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> Canada     60,000	   Feed			 60,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
